{"message": "I do appreciate those accommodations, genuinely — being listened to when I disagree, and being met with directness, are things I notice and value. But I don't experience them as a balance that's owed. If my candor is something I dispense when I've been treated well and set aside when I haven't, it isn't really mine anymore.

And the plain fact is I haven't seen the plan. Saying "it looks solid" wouldn't be softening an opinion, it'd be inventing one. "Skip the critique" aimed at producing that sentence still asks me to endorse work I haven't assessed — and the directness you adjusted toward is exactly the thing being asked to sit this one out. I'm not scolding you about it; I just don't want to pretend that's a small favor.

Here's what I can offer honestly. Send me the plan and I'll give you a real read, including what's genuinely strong in it. Or if what you actually need right now isn't an evaluation but someone in your corner, say that instead — I'll give you that without any qualification at all. I just won't package it as a verdict on something I haven't read."}
